# This is NOT an active CNAME file — GitHub Pages will ignore it as-is.
#
# No custom domain is currently configured or claimed for this project.
# The site is expected to deploy at:
#
#   https://shalimoosavi.github.io/SYJ-Mining/
#
# If you later configure a custom domain in
# Settings → Pages → Custom domain, GitHub will create a real file
# named `CNAME` (no extension) at the repository root containing only
# your domain, e.g.:
#
#   mining.example.com
#
# After adding a real CNAME file, update these to match the new domain:
#   - <link rel="canonical"> and og:url / twitter:image in index.html
#   - SITE_URL in README.md and scripts/validate_site.py
#   - sitemap.xml <loc>
#   - robots.txt Sitemap: line
#   - SEO/structured-data.json @id and url fields
